import WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck

/-!
# Forward-space automaton certificate for the Aztec and Noir BN254 permutation, width four

Data and kernel checks for the middle bound of `WideTrail.Poseidon2.AztecBN254Middle`. The
partial-round matrix is the internal layer `diag(d) + J` of `WideTrail.Poseidon2.AztecBN254`,
with `d` the stored array `internalDiag` (the diagonal entries of the matrix are `d_i + 1`), over
`ZMod p` with `p = fieldModulus` (the value of `Poseidon2.BN254.modulus`); the S-box is on
coordinate `0`. The automaton covers a window of `14` partial rounds.

* `internalRows`: the internal matrix `diag(d) + J`, row `i` holding the coefficients of output
  coordinate `i`: entry `(i, i)` is `d_i + 1` and every other entry is `1`. `internalDiagonal`:
  the stored array `d` (`internalDiag`). `externalRows`: the external matrix `hlMat4` of
  `WideTrail.Poseidon2.HorizenLabsM4`, by rows.
* `states`: a forward-space automaton (`Hades.AutomatonCheck.AState`) with `255` states. State `0`
  has no functional (it stands for every difference), potential `3` and depth `0`. Every other
  state `q` has a depth between `1` and `14` and one, two or three functionals, and stands for
  the differences on which they vanish: a subspace that contains every difference with which a
  trail whose first `depth q` rounds have one fixed activity pattern can enter round `depth q`.
  Its potential is `3` minus its number of functionals. The `191` states of depth less than `14`
  have both transitions checked: an active round always has a successor, and an inactive round
  has none exactly from the `63` states with three functionals. The `64` states of depth `14`
  have no successor.
* `windowStates`, `windowOutputs`: a trail through `14` rounds with the internal matrix and the
  S-box at coordinate `0`: row `n` of `windowStates` is the difference entering round `n`, entry
  `n` of `windowOutputs` the S-box output difference of round `n`. Its active rounds are the even
  rounds from `2` to `12`, so `6` of them.
* `trailStates`, `trailSboxOutputs`: a trail through the `64` rounds of the Aztec schedule (`4`
  full rounds with the external matrix, `56` partial rounds with the internal matrix and the
  S-box at coordinate `0`, `4` full rounds): row `n` of `trailStates` is the difference entering
  round `n`, row `n` of `trailSboxOutputs` the difference after its S-box layer.
* `middleStates`, `middleOutputs`: rows `4, …, 60` of `trailStates` and coordinate `0` of rows
  `4, …, 59` of `trailSboxOutputs`, read as a trail through the `56` partial rounds.

The checks, each by `decide +kernel`:

* `automaton_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkAll` passes for the window of `14` rounds with
  `internalRows`, the S-box at coordinate `0` and start state `0`; `start_pot`: the start state
  has potential `3`, so the certificate gives `(14 + 1 - 3) / 2 = 6`.
* `window_trail_check`: `Hades.RelationCheck.checkTrail` passes for `windowStates` and
  `windowOutputs` with `internalDiagonal`, over `14` rounds.
* `trail_check`: `Hades.AutomatonCheck.checkHadesTrail` passes for the `4 + 56 + 4` rounds;
  `trail_weight`: the charged weight of that trail is `47`.
* `middle_trail_check`: `Hades.RelationCheck.checkTrail` passes for `middleStates` and
  `middleOutputs` with `internalDiagonal`, over the `56` partial rounds.

The data were computed outside Lean from the literals of the instance files (`internalDiag` of
`WideTrail.Poseidon2.AztecBN254`, `hlMat4` of `WideTrail.Poseidon2.HorizenLabsM4`); nothing
depends on how they were found, since the checks are complete. This file imports only
`WideTrail.Hades.AutomatonCheck`, which imports only `WideTrail.Hades.RelationCheck` and through
it `Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic`.

## What is not claimed

The checks are statements about lists of natural numbers. What they mean for trails is proved in
`WideTrail.Hades.Automaton` and `WideTrail.Hades.WindowRelation`, and applied in
`WideTrail.Poseidon2.AztecBN254Middle` and `WideTrail.Poseidon2.Checks.AztecBN254Middle`. The
automaton certifies `6` for one window of `14` rounds, not a bound for the `56` partial rounds
as a whole. The witness trails are trails in the `IsTrail` model (supports, masks and linear maps
only); they are not claimed to be realised by an input pair or a key.
-/

